# Copy to .env.local and adjust, or export the variable in your shell.
#
# VITE_API_URL tells the frontend where the backend lives. Vite inlines this at BUILD
# time, not at runtime: a value baked into a production build cannot be changed by
# editing this file afterwards, it needs a rebuild.
#
#   empty            Use the dev server's /api proxy (vite.config.ts forwards /api/*).
#                    This is the right setting for local work with a backend on :8080.
#   http://host:port Point directly at a backend, including from `vite preview`.
#                    Required for preview and for any deployment that is not on the
#                    same origin, because the proxy only exists in `npm run dev`.
#
VITE_API_URL=
